IMPORT `oa1-helpers`

-- Old Age Security Act, Part IV, "Effect of Waiver", "Inviting Applications", "Incapacity", "Death" and "Erroneous Advice or
-- Administrative Error" (ss 26.1, 26.2, 28.1, 29, 30, 31, 32): when an application is deemed made, and when a late or
-- someone else's application counts.
-- The Hohfeldian pairs are in NOTES.md ("Jural relations"). In brief: the Minister's power to deem an application made earlier
-- (28.1) is the person's liability; the person's right to be put in the position they would have been in (32) is the Minister's duty;
-- the Minister's power to certify a death (31) is the person's liability.

§ `Effect of Waiver`

-- s 26.1: "the application is deemed to have been made by the applicant on the day on which the requirement is waived".
-- src:827 | 26.1 When the requirement for an application for a benefit is waived by the Minister under this Act, the application is deemed to have been made by the applicant on the day on which the requirement is waived and, for greater certainty, the applicant shall not be paid that benefit for any month that is more than 11 months before the month in which the application is deemed to have been made.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 26.1 (src:827)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application for a benefit is waived by the Minister under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 11 (piece oa2); section 19 (piece oa2); section 21 (piece oa2): the waivers for a supplement or an allowance (section 5(4) is this piece's)
      `the day on which the requirement is waived` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 26.1: the day on which the application is deemed to have been made` `the requirement for an application for a benefit is waived by the Minister under this Act` `the day on which the requirement is waived` MEANS
    IF `the requirement for an application for a benefit is waived by the Minister under this Act`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the requirement is waived`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "the applicant shall not be paid that benefit for any month that is more than 11 months before the month in which the application is
-- deemed to have been made". TRUE means this limit does not bar the month; it does not say the benefit is payable.
-- src:827 | 26.1 When the requirement for an application for a benefit is waived by the Minister under this Act, the application is deemed to have been made by the applicant on the day on which the requirement is waived and, for greater certainty, the applicant shall not be paid that benefit for any month that is more than 11 months before the month in which the application is deemed to have been made.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 26.1 (src:827)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application is deemed to have been made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26.1: the limit of 11 months before the month of the deemed application does not bar the benefit for the month` month `the day on which the application is deemed to have been made` MEANS
    (`the number of months from the month containing` month `to the month containing` `the day on which the application is deemed to have been made`) AT MOST 11

§ `Inviting Applications`

-- s 26.2: the Minister's power, with the person's liability that their information is collected and used for the purpose.
-- src:831 | 26.2 The Minister may invite persons to make an application for benefits under this Act and may, for that purpose, collect personal information and make available or use personal information available to him or her under this Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 26.2 (src:831)
GIVEN `the purpose is to invite persons to make an application for benefits under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 26.2: the Minister may collect, make available or use personal information for the purpose` `the purpose is to invite persons to make an application for benefits under this Act` MEANS
    `the purpose is to invite persons to make an application for benefits under this Act`

§ `Incapacity`

-- s 28.1(1) and (2) share one effect: the later of two months, the month before the first month the benefit could have been paid and the
-- month the Minister considers the last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced. The first month is passed as any date in it.
-- src:855 | 28.1 (1) Where an application for a benefit is made on behalf of a person and the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of that person, that the person was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the person’s own behalf on the day on which the application was actually made, the Minister may deem the application to have been made in the month preceding the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid or in the month that the Minister considers the person’s last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced, whichever is the later.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, ss 28.1(1), 28.1(2) (src:855) (src:863)
GIVEN `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` IS A DATE -- out of range: section 11 (piece oa2); section 19 (piece oa2); section 21 (piece oa2): when the benefit could first have been paid (section 8 is this piece's)
      `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 28.1: the month in which the application may be deemed to have been made` `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` MEANS
    `oa1: the later of two dates`
        (`the first day of the month containing` (`the day that is` (`a limit in months` 1) `before` (`the first day of the month containing` `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid`)))
        (`the first day of the month containing` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced`)

-- (1): made on behalf of a person; the Minister is satisfied, on evidence, that the person was incapable of forming or expressing an
-- intention to make an application on the day it was actually made.
-- src:855 | 28.1 (1) Where an application for a benefit is made on behalf of a person and the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of that person, that the person was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the person’s own behalf on the day on which the application was actually made, the Minister may deem the application to have been made in the month preceding the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid or in the month that the Minister considers the person’s last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced, whichever is the later.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 28.1(1) (src:855)
GIVEN `the application for a benefit is made on behalf of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of that person, that the person was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the person's own behalf on the day on which the application was actually made` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: section 11 (piece oa2); section 19 (piece oa2); section 21 (piece oa2): when the benefit could first have been paid (section 8 is this piece's)
      `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` IS A DATE
      `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 28.1(1): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` `the application for a benefit is made on behalf of a person` `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of that person, that the person was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the person's own behalf on the day on which the application was actually made` `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` MEANS
    IF     `the application for a benefit is made on behalf of a person`
       AND `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of that person, that the person was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the person's own behalf on the day on which the application was actually made`
    THEN JUST (`s 28.1: the month in which the application may be deemed to have been made` `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2)(c): the application was made (i) within the period that begins on the day the person ceased to be incapable and has the same
-- number of days as the period of incapacity, but not more than twelve months, or (ii) where that period is fewer than thirty days,
-- not more than one month after the month in which the person ceased to be incapable. The period of N days that begins on a day ends N-1 days
-- later; twelve months from a day end on the day before the same day a year on (fork OA1-F10 of NOTES.md).
-- src:860 | (c) the application was made
-- src:861 | (i) within the period beginning on the day on which that person had ceased to be incapable and comprising the same number of days, not exceeding twelve months, as in the period of incapacity, or
-- src:862 | (ii) where the period referred to in subparagraph (i) comprises fewer than thirty days, not more than one month after the month in which that person ceased to be so incapable,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 28.1(2)(c) (src:860-862)
GIVEN `the day on which the person ceased to be incapable` IS A DATE
      `the number of days in the period of incapacity` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the application was actually made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 28.1(2)(c): the application was made in time` `the day on which the person ceased to be incapable` `the number of days in the period of incapacity` `the day on which the application was actually made` MEANS
        `the day on which the application was actually made` AT MOST lastDayOfPeriod
    OR  (    periodDays LESS THAN 30
         AND (`the number of months from the month containing` `the day on which the person ceased to be incapable` `to the month containing` `the day on which the application was actually made`) AT MOST 1)
    WHERE
        twelveMonthsLastDay MEANS (`the day that is` (`a limit in months` 12) `after` `the day on which the person ceased to be incapable`) MINUS 1
        lastDayOfPeriod MEANS `oa1: the earlier of two dates` (`the day on which the person ceased to be incapable` PLUS (`the number of days in the period of incapacity` MINUS 1)) twelveMonthsLastDay
        periodDays MEANS (`the number of days from` `the day on which the person ceased to be incapable` `to` lastDayOfPeriod) PLUS 1

