`s 28.1(2): the month in which the Minister may deem the application to have been made` `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of that person, that the person was incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application before the day on which the application was actually made` `the day on which the person ceased to be incapable` `the number of days in the period of incapacity` `the day on which the application was actually made` `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` MEANS
