§ `Death`

-- s 29(1): an application for a pension that would have been payable to a deceased person, within one year after the death.
-- "within one year after": the same day a year on is still within the year (fork OA1-F15 of NOTES.md).
-- src:871 | 29 (1) Despite anything in this Act, an application for a pension that would have been payable to a deceased person who, before their death, would have been entitled, on approval of an application, to payment of that pension under this Act may be made within one year after the person’s death by the estate or succession, by the liquidator, executor or administrator of the estate or succession or heir of that person or by any person that may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 29(1) (src:871)
GIVEN `the deceased person would, before their death, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: the Regulations (piece oa3): none prescribes a person for section 29(1)
      `the applicant is the estate or succession, the liquidator, executor or administrator of the estate or succession, an heir of that person, or a person that may be prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the person's death` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29(1): an application may be made for the pension that would have been payable to the deceased person` `the deceased person would, before their death, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the pension` `the applicant is the estate or succession, the liquidator, executor or administrator of the estate or succession, an heir of that person, or a person that may be prescribed by regulation` `the day of the person's death` `the day on which the application is made` MEANS
        `the deceased person would, before their death, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the pension`
    AND `the applicant is the estate or succession, the liquidator, executor or administrator of the estate or succession, an heir of that person, or a person that may be prescribed by regulation`
    AND `the day on which the application is made` AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in years` 1) `after` `the day of the person's death`)

-- (2): the pension is paid to the estate or succession or to a prescribed person.
-- src:873 | (2) If an application is made under subsection (1), the pension that would have been payable to a deceased person referred to in that subsection shall be paid to the estate or succession or to any person that may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 29(2) (src:873)
GIVEN `an application is made under subsection 29(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      payee IS A Party
      `the payee is a person that may be prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29(2): the pension is to be paid to the payee` `an application is made under subsection 29(1)` payee `the payee is a person that may be prescribed by regulation` MEANS
        `an application is made under subsection 29(1)`
    AND (payee EQUALS Estate OR `the payee is a person that may be prescribed by regulation`)

-- (3): "deemed to have been received on the date of the death".
