    IF `an application is made under subsection 29(1)`
    THEN JUST `the day of the person's death`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 30(1): the survivor's application, within one year after the death, despite paragraph 19(6)(b).
-- "within one year after": the same day a year on is still within the year (fork OA1-F15 of NOTES.md).
-- src:877 | 30 (1) Despite paragraph 19(6)(b), if a person dies and the person’s survivor would have been entitled to an allowance under section 19 had the survivor and the deceased person made a joint application for it before the death of the deceased person, the survivor may make application for an allowance under section 19 within one year after the death of the deceased person.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 30(1) (src:877)
