      `the day of the death of the deceased person` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the survivor makes application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 30(1): the survivor may make application for an allowance under section 19` `the survivor would have been entitled to an allowance under section 19 had the survivor and the deceased person made a joint application for it before the death of the deceased person` `the day of the death of the deceased person` `the day on which the survivor makes application` MEANS
        `the survivor would have been entitled to an allowance under section 19 had the survivor and the deceased person made a joint application for it before the death of the deceased person`
    AND `the day on which the survivor makes application` AT MOST (`the day that is` (`a limit in years` 1) `after` `the day of the death of the deceased person`)

-- (2): considered as a joint application received on the date of the death.
