-- s 31(1): the Minister's certificate. The Minister must be of the opinion that the circumstances of the disappearance raise, beyond a
-- reasonable doubt, a presumption of death; the person is then deemed for all purposes of the Act to have died on the stated date.
-- src:882 | 31 (1) Where an applicant or beneficiary has disappeared under circumstances that, in the opinion of the Minister, raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption that the applicant or beneficiary is dead, the Minister may issue a certificate declaring that the applicant or beneficiary is presumed to be dead and stating the date on which the death is presumed to have occurred, and thereupon the applicant or beneficiary shall be deemed for all purposes of this Act to have died on the date so stated in the certificate.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 31(1) (src:882)
GIVEN `the applicant or beneficiary has disappeared under circumstances that, in the opinion of the Minister, raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption that the applicant or beneficiary is dead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister issues a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the death is presumed to have occurred, as stated in the certificate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 31(1): the day on which the applicant or beneficiary is deemed to have died` `the applicant or beneficiary has disappeared under circumstances that, in the opinion of the Minister, raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption that the applicant or beneficiary is dead` `the Minister issues a certificate` `the date on which the death is presumed to have occurred, as stated in the certificate` MEANS
    IF     `the applicant or beneficiary has disappeared under circumstances that, in the opinion of the Minister, raise beyond a reasonable doubt a presumption that the applicant or beneficiary is dead`
       AND `the Minister issues a certificate`
    THEN JUST `the date on which the death is presumed to have occurred, as stated in the certificate`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (2): a new certificate stating a different date replaces the old one; the date in the latest certificate is the date of death.
-- src:884 | (2) If, after issuing a certificate under subsection (1), the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the date of death is different from that stated in the certificate, the Minister may revoke the certificate and issue a new certificate stating a different date, in which case the applicant or beneficiary shall be deemed for all purposes of this Act to have died on the date so stated in the new certificate.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 31(2) (src:884)
GIVEN `the date stated in the certificate issued under subsection 31(1)` IS A DATE
      `the date stated in a new certificate issued after the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the date of death is different` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 31(2): the day on which the applicant or beneficiary is deemed to have died` `the date stated in the certificate issued under subsection 31(1)` `the date stated in a new certificate issued after the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the date of death is different` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date stated in a new certificate issued after the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the date of death is different`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date stated in the certificate issued under subsection 31(1)`
    WHEN JUST newDate THEN newDate

-- (3): where the person presumed dead reappears, the Minister shall revoke the certificate forthwith and cause the benefits to be
-- reinstated effective the month following the date of presumed death, subject to eligibility.
-- src:886 | (3) If, after issuing a certificate under this section, the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the applicant or beneficiary named in the certificate is alive, the Minister shall forthwith revoke the certificate and cause that person’s benefits to be re-instated effective the month following the date of the person’s presumed death stated in the certificate, subject to the provisions of this Act relating to the person’s eligibility to receive those benefits.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 31(3) (src:886)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the applicant or beneficiary named in the certificate is alive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the person's presumed death stated in the certificate` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 31(3): the month effective which the person's benefits are reinstated` `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the applicant or beneficiary named in the certificate is alive` `the date of the person's presumed death stated in the certificate` MEANS
    IF `the Minister is satisfied from new information or evidence that the applicant or beneficiary named in the certificate is alive`
    THEN JUST (`the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the date of the person's presumed death stated in the certificate`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (4): "the Minister is not bound by the issuance or revocation of a death certificate by any other authority".
-- src:888 | (4) For the purposes of this section, the Minister is not bound by the issuance or revocation of a death certificate by any other authority.
