§ `Erroneous Advice or Administrative Error`

-- s 32: the Minister shall take such remedial action as the Minister considers appropriate; the person's claim is to be put in the position
-- they would be in had the advice not been given or the error not been made.
-- src:892 | 32 Where the Minister is satisfied that, as a result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act, any person has been denied a benefit, or a portion of a benefit, to which that person would have been entitled under this Act, the Minister shall take such remedial action as the Minister considers appropriate to place the person in the position that the person would be in under this Act had the erroneous advice not been given or the administrative error not been made.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 32 (src:892)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that, as a result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act, the person has been denied a benefit, or a portion of a benefit, to which the person would have been entitled under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32: the Minister shall take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in under this Act had the erroneous advice not been given or the administrative error not been made` `the Minister is satisfied that, as a result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act, the person has been denied a benefit, or a portion of a benefit, to which the person would have been entitled under this Act` MEANS
    `the Minister is satisfied that, as a result of erroneous advice or administrative error in the administration of this Act, the person has been denied a benefit, or a portion of a benefit, to which the person would have been entitled under this Act`
